given-names>DA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Chronic radiodermatitis following cardiac catheterization</article-title><source>Arch Dermatol</source><year>1996</year><volume>132</volume><fpage>663</fpage><lpage>667</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archderm.132.6.663</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Lichtenstein DA, Klapholz L, Vardy DA, et al (1996) Chronic radiodermatitis following cardiac catheterization. Arch Dermatol 132:663&#x02013;67 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8651716</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sovik</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Klow</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hellesnes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Radiation-induced skin injury after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. Case report</article-title><source>Acta Radiol</source><year>1996</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>305</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3109/02841859609177655</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Sovik E, Klow NE, Hellesnes J, et al (1996) Radiation-induced skin injury after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. Case report. Acta Radiol 37:305&#x02013;06 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8845258</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knautz</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Abele</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Radiodermatitis after transjugular intrahepatic portosystemic shunt</article-title><source>South Med J</source><year>1997</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>352</fpage><lpage>356</lpage><pub-i